{"approved_definition": "Restraint of actions, inclinations, and impulses likely to upset or harm others and violate social expectations or norms. Derives from the requirement that individuals inhibit inclinations that might disrupt and undermine smooth interaction and group functioning (cf. Freud, 1930; Kohn & Schooler, 1983; Parsons, 1951).", "core_value": "conformity", "sources": [{"entry_id": "dbe2c53d:entry:4", "journal_entry": "Family group chat exploded today. My uncle Hernando posted a news article about the Guaviare deforestation — same issue the march is about — and wrote "sad but what can you do, these people need to eat." I started typing a response three times. Deleted all of them.

It's not that I disagree entirely — the economics of it are real and I've seen the poverty firsthand. But the framing drives me insane. "What can you do" as if there are no choices, no policies, no one responsible. I wanted to write about the logging companies, the lack of enforcement, the families who actually live there being displaced. But Hernando is my mother's brother and I can already picture the awkward silence at Easter dinner if I go off in the group chat.

So I sent a sad emoji and closed the app. Mature. Professional. Utterly hollow. Patricia would have posted a five-paragraph essay with citations. I admire that and also cannot imagine being that person in my own family. The mural for the march — that I can do. Words in the chat where my grandmother can see them — that's different somehow, and I hate that it's different.", "nudge_response": null}, {"entry_id": "dbe2c53d:entry:1", "journal_entry": "Good day at the workshop. One of the teenagers, David, showed up with a collage about his neighborhood flooding last year — garbage and river water mixed together. He made it beautiful without sanitizing it. I wish I had his nerve sometimes.", "nudge_response": null}, {"entry_id": "dbe2c53d:entry:7", "journal_entry": "Long day prepping supplies for Friday. Shoulders ache. Didn't think about the committee or my mother or the march. Just mixed pigments and cleaned brushes. Sometimes that's enough.", "nudge_response": null}], "user_phrase": "Being someone others can count on to do the right thing"}
